Package: astro-camera
Version: 2.0.0
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: armhf
Maintainer: Aviral Verma <aviralverma-8877@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/aviralverma-8877/astro_camera
Depends: python3 (>= 3.7), python3-pil, python3-numpy, python3-opencv, python3-picamera2, python3-spidev, python3-flask, hostapd, dnsmasq
Recommends: python3-lgpio
Suggests: samba
Description: High-performance Raspberry Pi astrophotography camera system
 Astro Camera transforms your Raspberry Pi into a standalone astrophotography
 platform with physical button controls and an integrated LCD display.
 .
 Features:
  - RAW & JPEG capture with configurable exposure settings
  - Manual controls: ISO, shutter speed, multi-shot sequences
  - Live preview with zoom and crosshair overlay
  - Built-in gallery for reviewing images on LCD
  - USB mass storage mode (Pi Zero models)
  - Physical button interface with 8 buttons
  - 128x128 LCD display (Waveshare 1.44")
  - Efficient operation with minimal CPU usage
  - Pi 5 compatible with automatic GPIO backend selection
